  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: “Blinding” headache for the past 3 days.\n• Symptoms:\n  – Onset/Duration: Sudden onset upon waking; persistent for 3 days.\n  – Location: Diffuse but worst over right eye.\n  – Character/Severity: Constant, 8/10 at worst, decreases to 5/10 with ibuprofen but never fully resolves.\n  – Associated features: Photophobia, transient “shooting lights” / visual disturbance, mild nausea (no vomiting), no focal neurologic deficits (numbness, weakness, speech changes), no fever, no sinus/respiratory symptoms.\n  – Aggravating: Bright light, sudden standing/head movement.\n  – Alleviating: Partial relief with ibuprofen, able to sleep (headache does not wake her at night).\n• Past medical history: Essentially none; vague childhood “pain” that resolved.\n• Medications/Allergies:\n  – Combined oral contraceptive pill (started 1 yr ago; exact brand not specified).\n  – PRN ibuprofen; no other drugs.\n  – No known drug or other allergies.\n• Family history: Mother suffers from migraines with vomiting.\n• Social history: Lives alone, works from home. Non-smoker. Alcohol ~3 drinks once weekly. No recreational drugs. No recent travel.\n• Vital signs / exam findings: None performed yet (tele-visit only). Patient afebrile by history; last BP check 1 yr ago “normal.”\n• Labs/imaging: None obtained/mentioned.",
